  "title": "Temple of Bel, Palmyra",
  "summary": "The Temple of Bel was the principal temple of Palmyra in modern Syria, dedicated to Bel and dated in sources to 32 CE; EBSCO says it was rebuilt in the course of the second century. Explosives destroyed it on 30 August 2015, according to UNESCO, after the Islamic State began destroying Palmyra's religious sites.",
